      {
        "title": "GvpA",
        "extract": "<p><b>GvpA</b> is a gas vesicle structural protein found in different phyla of bacteria and archaea for example in <i>Halobacterium salinarum</i> or <i>Haloferax mediterranei</i>. Gas vesicles are small, hollow, gas filled protein structures found in several cyanobacterial and archaebacterial microorganisms. They allow the positioning of the bacteria at a favourable depth for growth.</p>",
